$$ \sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} = \sqrt{8(8-5)(8-5)(8-6)} = \sqrt{8(3)(3)(2)} = \sqrt{144} = 12. $$
Since the area of $\triangle ABC$ is 12, we have $\frac{1}{2} \cdot AC \cdot BE = 12$, so $\frac{1}{2} \cdot 6 \cdot BE = 12$, which gives $BE = \frac{24}{6} = 4$.
