Then $\sin(\angle C) = \sqrt{1 - \cos^2(\angle C)} = \sqrt{1 - (\frac{3}{5})^2} = \sqrt{1 - \frac{9}{25}} = \sqrt{\frac{16}{25}} = \frac{4}{5}$.
The area of $\triangle DEC = \frac{1}{2} \cdot CE \cdot CD \cdot \sin(\angle C) = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 3 \cdot 2.5 \cdot \frac{4}{5} = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 3 \cdot \frac{5}{2} \cdot \frac{4}{5} = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{60}{10} = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 6 = 3$.

