Let the width of the rectangular pool be $w = 6$ m, the length be $l = 12$ m, and the depth be $d = 4$ m. The pool is half full of water.
The volume of the pool is $V = w \times l \times d = 6 \times 12 \times 4 = 288 \text{ m}^3$.
Since the pool is half full, the volume of water is $\frac{1}{2} V = \frac{1}{2} \times 288 = 144 \text{ m}^3$.

\boxed{144 \text{ m}^3}
