\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{amssymb}

The volume of the original cube is $2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm} = 8 \text{ cm}^3$.
The volume of the larger cube is $8 \text{ cm}^3 + 19 \text{ cm}^3 = 27 \text{ cm}^3$.
Let $s$ be the side length of the larger cube. Then $s^3 = 27 \text{ cm}^3$.
Therefore, $s = \sqrt[3]{27 \text{ cm}^3} = 3 \text{ cm}$.

The length of the edge of the new cube is 3 cm.
